 "_about": "Frozen regression probes for resolve_jurisdiction — the Phase 1 exit criterion from docs/plans/2026-08-12-gwinnett-index-build-plan.md, in point form. 10 points inside Duluth city limits, 10 in unincorporated Gwinnett within 3 km of the Duluth boundary: the belt where a 'Duluth, GA' mailing address is NOT the City of Duluth, which is the product's core claim.",
 "_method": "Sampled 2026-08-17 from resolver_probe (the 1,915-point scored fixture taken from the county's own zoning layers), keeping only points the resolver answered correctly at HIGH confidence on that date — this file pins that behavior, it does not measure accuracy. The unincorporated ten were additionally required to lie within 3,000 m of the Duluth city boundary (ST_DWithin on geography) and outside it (NOT ST_Within). Points are probes by design, not addresses: the public /v1/resolve geocodes first, and a geocoder's drift is not the resolver's regression. expected_citation pins the jurisdiction row's code_citation as returned BY the function, because /j/duluth rendering 'Code: not indexed here' over an 858-section corpus was a live wrong answer found 2026-08-17 — a null citation for an indexed jurisdiction must fail this test, not ship.",
